            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h4>Streaming Data Analysis</h4>
              <ul>
                <li>Stream tweets to a JSON file</li>
                <li>Stream tweets to MongoDB</li>
              </ul>
            </motion.div>
          </motion.div>
        </motion.section>

        {/* Amazon EMR */}
        <motion.section
          className={`${styles.emr} ${styles.section}`}
          initial="hidden"
          whileInView="visible"
          viewport={VIEWPORT}
          variants={fadeUp}
        >
          <h2>Big Data Processing Assignment Help with Amazon EMR</h2>
          <div className={styles.emrContent}>
            <EmrArchitectureViz />
            <div>
              <p>
                Amazon EMR is a managed cluster platform that simplifies running Big Data frameworks
                such as Apache Hadoop and Apache Spark on AWS to process and analyze vast amounts of
                data. Combined with open-source projects like Apache Hive and Apache Pig, it supports
                analytics and business-intelligence workloads.
              </p>
              <p>
                You can also use Amazon EMR to move large amounts of data into and out of other AWS
                data stores, such as Amazon S3 and Amazon DynamoDB.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4>Common tasks in Big Data processing with Amazon EMR</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Understanding clusters and nodes</li>
              <li>Submitting work to a cluster</li>
              <li>Processing data</li>
              <li>Understanding the cluster lifecycle</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </motion.section>

        {/* MapReduce */}
        <motion.section
          className={`${styles.mapReduce} ${styles.section}`}
          initial="hidden"
          whileInView="visible"
          viewport={VIEWPORT}
          variants={fadeUp}
        >
          <h2>MapReduce Assignment Help</h2>
          <p>Hadoop is a data management and distributed processing system with several core components:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>HDFS — a file system that distributes data across many machines</li>
            <li>MapReduce — for batch parallel computing</li>
          </ul>
          <p>MapReduce has two main tasks:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Map</li>
            <li>Reduce</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Data blocks distributed across machines are processed by Map tasks in parallel, and results
            are aggregated in Reducers. MapReduce works only with key/value pairs.
          </p>
          <div className={styles.mapReduceDetail}>
            <div>
              <h4>MapReduce Key/Value Pairs</h4>
              <p>The data exchanged between Map and Reduce — and throughout the entire job — are (key, value) pairs:</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>A key</strong> can be any type of data: integer, text, and so on.</li>
                <li><strong>A value</strong> can also be any type of data.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>For example:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>A text file is a set of (line number, line) pairs.</li>
                <li>A weather file is a set of (date and time, temperature) pairs.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4>MapReduce — Word Count Example</h4>
              <MapReduceWordCountViz />
            </div>
          </div>
        </motion.section>

        {/* Domains */}
        <motion.section
          className={`${styles.domains} ${styles.section}`}
          initial="hidden"
          whileInView="visible"
          viewport={VIEWPORT}
          variants={fadeUp}
        >
          <h2>Domain-Specific Examples of Big Data</h2>
          <motion.div
            className={styles.domainGrid}
            initial="hidden"
            whileInView="visible"
            viewport={VIEWPORT}
            variants={stagger}
          >
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Financial (Credit Risk Modeling, Fraud Detection)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Credit Risk Modeling:</strong> Banks and financial institutions use credit risk
                modeling to score applications and predict whether a borrower will default. Big Data
                systems power the models behind these decisions.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Web (Web Analytics, Content Recommendation)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Content Recommendation:</strong> These applications lean on Big Data systems to
                recommend new content based on user preferences and interests.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Environment (Weather, Air &amp; Noise Pollution, Forest Fires, River Floods)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Air Pollution Monitoring:</strong> Sensor networks track emissions from
                factories and vehicles; the collected data informs pollution-control decisions.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Healthcare (Epidemiological Surveillance, Real-Time Monitoring)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Real-Time Health Monitoring:</strong> Real-time analysis of fast-moving data from
                wearables and in-hospital devices supports patient monitoring and adverse-event
                prediction.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Internet of Things (Intrusion Detection, Smart Parking, Smart Irrigation)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Intrusion Detection:</strong> Security cameras and sensors detect intrusions and
                raise alerts.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Smart Parking:</strong> Per-slot sensors report occupancy to a cloud-based Big
                Data analytics backend.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Logistics &amp; Transportation (Shipment Monitoring, Route Scheduling)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Shipment Monitoring:</strong> Temperature, pressure, and humidity sensors detect
                spoilage in fresh-food containers in transit.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Retail (Recommendations, Store Layout, Demand Forecasting)</h5>
              <p><strong>Customer Recommendations:</strong> Analyzing demographic, purchase, and feedback data to predict preferences.</p>
              <p><strong>Store Layout Optimization:</strong> Shopping-pattern and feedback data inform better store layouts.</p>
              <p><strong>Demand Forecasting:</strong> Purchase patterns predict demand and sale volumes.</p>
            </motion.div>
            <motion.div variants={fadeUp}>
              <h5>Industry (Machine Diagnosis, Production Planning)</h5>
              <p>
                <strong>Production Planning and Control:</strong> Sensor data across the production
                process supports real-time planning and early problem detection.
              </p>
            </motion.div>
          </motion.div>
        </motion.section>

        {/* Industry applications */}
        <motion.section
          className={`${styles.industry} ${styles.section}`}
          initial="hidden"
          whileInView="visible"
          viewport={VIEWPORT}
