        >
          <h2>Industry Use &amp; Applications</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Crime prediction</li>
            <li>Disease prediction</li>
            <li>Simulating and predicting traffic patterns</li>
            <li>Modeling natural language</li>
            <li>Fraud detection</li>
            <li>Sentiment analysis at scale</li>
            <li>Deceit recognition</li>
            <li>Predicting audience interests</li>
            <li>On-demand scheduling for digital media distribution</li>
            <li>Extracting insight from customer reviews</li>
            <li>Effective ad targeting</li>
            <li>Social media data analysis with Spark</li>
            <li>Applying classification models to tweets</li>
            <li>Real-time tweet analysis with the Spark Streaming library</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Applications of Big Data in Education</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Customized and Dynamic Learning Programs:</strong> Individual learning history shapes personalized programs that improve student outcomes.</li>
            <li><strong>Reframing Course Material:</strong> Real-time monitoring of how students engage with material informs better course design.</li>
            <li><strong>Grading Systems:</strong> Deeper analysis of student data has driven new grading approaches.</li>
            <li><strong>Career Prediction:</strong> Analyzing a student's progress, strengths, and interests helps identify suitable career paths.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Big Data has helped move education away from a one-size-fits-all model, contributing
            directly to better e-learning solutions.
          </p>
        </motion.section>

        {/* Case Studies */}
        <motion.section
          className={`${styles.caseStudies} ${styles.section}`}
